From 6544d5395d14708c0b217737ec05554ae213079c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 17:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Replace manual-paste platform IDs with live-fetched pickers

Every place a connected API key still forced a hand-typed id from a
third-party dashboard now derives it instead, mirroring the pattern
this app already used for Klaviyo/GHL/Booking:

- Cold Open Send Connect: campaign id and ICP slug are now pickers
  sourced from each ESP's listCampaigns() and ICP Lock's saved ICPs,
  instead of a free-text "the real campaign id from your ESP" field.
- Win-Back: HubSpot Portal ID auto-detects from HubSpot's account-info
  API (a wrong hand-typed value silently drops inbound-reply webhook
  routing), shown as a detected badge with a manual override.
- edit-stack-settings.tsx (the live per-client settings panel, not the
  unreachable engagements/new wizard): one consolidated route resolves
  the engagement's already-saved credential server-side and lists live
  options for Klaviyo, Mailchimp, ConvertKit, ActiveCampaign (lists +
  automations), HubSpot workflows, Webflow (sites + collections),
  Vercel (projects + teams), Twilio (messaging services + numbers),
  and Google Sheets (spreadsheets + tabs).

Fields left as typed input are the credential's own scoping key,
required before any list call can be made (GHL Location ID, Twilio
Account SID, ActiveCampaign base URL) or have no listable endpoint
(Hyros account id).

